WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.353
A race doesn't always run from Go to the line. You might pause, leave, lose the

00:00:07.353 --> 00:00:08.438
bike, or win.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.820
Against bots, the bar has Leave. Solo, it has Pause and End. Either way out opens

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.056
Race Setup at once, with no confirmation, and earns no XP.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.513
Only a solo race pauses. The clock, the distance and the standings hold, and the

00:00:25.513 --> 00:00:27.759
card blocks none of the buttons.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.610
Resume carries the race on. So does pedalling again, once you have stopped, so the

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.173
stroke under your press never undoes it.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.331
If the bike stops answering, an alert says so with Reconnect. You coast, your speed

00:00:46.331 --> 00:00:50.697
falling to a stop over fifteen seconds, the resistance buttons off.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.742
Back in time, the race carries on. Fifteen seconds without the bike, and the race

00:00:56.742 --> 00:01:01.218
ends as a DNF, never a silent stop, with a way back to Race Setup.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.667
Solo, nobody else is on your clock, so the race parks until the bike is back, then

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.869
carries on from where it stopped.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.843
The line is the map's distance. Cross it, and your finish time is the race clock,

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:20.025
your place is where you crossed, and Results opens.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.279
Pause works the same from a phone to a desktop, its button forty-eight pixels under

00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:28.201
your thumb.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:37.779
What the tests prove: eleven new behaviour specs, the coast and the finish line in

00:01:37.779 --> 00:01:41.284
unit tests, all green, and the first bundle unchanged.

00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:47.840
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:48.185 --> 00:01:52.697
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:54.368
every hill and interval.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:59.891
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:59.891 --> 00:02:05.339
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:02:05.339 --> 00:02:08.329
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:02:08.675 --> 00:02:11.167
A custom workout lives under Profile.
